I checked the 3.4.2 logmoves patch and it worked in 3.4.3 as it was.
Anyway, I made a new diff. The patch will append the turn counter in curly
braces to the end of a logfile / record entry, after the "killer" string, 
like this:
3.4.3 147 0 2 2 12 12 0 20031211 20031211 1 Rog Hum Fem Cha test,quit {197}
It also adds a tag {exp} or {wiz} to the logfile entry if you used explore
or wizard mode.


And I combined the extinct and showborn patches to a single patch for
3.4.3, like I somewhere mentioned I was going to do because they are so
closely related to each other.
The extinction patch lists extincted monsters among the genocided ones
when the game ends, marking them with "(extinct)".
The showborn patch shows the number of each monster created after the kill
counter in the "vanquished monsters" list when the game ends, if the
number is different from the kill counter, and at least one of them was
killed.
The lists now look like this:

Vanquished creatures
  a gecko
  a jackal
  a sewer rat
  a grid bug (3 created)
  2 lichens
  120 newts
  126 creatures vanquished.

Genocided or extincted species:
  newts (extinct)
1 species extincted.

